<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dunsterforce</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1918</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dunsterforce was a small Allied military mission of picked British and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">Dominion</a> officers and troops under Major-General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lionel-dunsterville">Lionel Dunsterville</a>, sent through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> in 1918 to organise resistance in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> after the collapse of the Russian army. It reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baku">Baku</a> in August 1918 to help the Centrocaspian Dictatorship defend the city against the Ottoman Army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, but withdrew on 14 September, the day before Baku fell.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dunsterforce.jpg" alt="Dunsterforce" width="320" height="247" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: United States Military Academy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Ottoman_Rail_Network_in_World_War_I.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
